    "description": "## Problem\n\nE-Transfer Email shows blank on Sign-Up records. The field maps from Player's E-Transfer Email field, which never receives data — the email CMS sends in the SLC payload IS the e-transfer email, landing in PersonEmail.\n\n## Current state\n\nPlayer carries three email fields: PersonEmail (populated via SLC), Secondary_Email__c, and E-Transfer Email (unpopulated, off the Player layout). Sign-Up displays the E-Transfer field, so it is always blank.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Replace E-Transfer Email with the Email field on the Sign-Up layout/component.\n2. Remove E-Transfer Email from any remaining layouts, popups, and SLC field mappings.\n3. Do NOT delete the fields (see open question).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Sign-Up record view shows the Player/SLC email under a single Email display.\n2. Negative: no layout, screen flow, or list view still references E-Transfer Email.\n3. Idempotency: n/a (display change).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* CMS API change to send a distinct e-transfer email (rejected option).\n\n## Open question (non-blocking)\n\nDeprecate the E-Transfer Email fields on Player/SLC/Sign-Up now, or keep dormant in case players can later set a separate e-transfer email in CMS?\n\n## Source\n\nEmily doc comment 2026-08-28: \"the email we send you is the e-transfer email… Player email = signup e-transfer email.\" [Feedback doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LOMrG0-0JchyP9wHrV4hMlBqh-gMq8YxknpySd5OJjY/edit)",
